<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Imperial Academy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">124 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Imperial Academy, or Taixue, was an institution established under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-han">Emperor Wu</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a> in 124 BCE to train officials in the Confucian classics. It helped make Confucian learning the basis of government service. It was an important foundation of the Han Dynasty's bureaucratic state.</p></div>
